<p>Too often compulsion effects are a lazy substitute for good writing. It's nice to be reminded that they can be employed very well indeed in the hands of a skilled author. Very creepy existential horror delivered via <em>excessive hugs.</em></p>
<p>I also want to applaud your journal entries here: I thought the pacing was excellent, telling the story evocatively and succinctly without feeling rushed or forced-marched. Very organic feel to it. You nearly had me in real tears with his line about not being able to escape by shooting up&#8212;that's some heartbreaking shit right there. Heartily upvoted!</p>
<p><sub><em>(edited for typos)</em></sub></p>

